    <!-- The app icon a reader chooses. Five faces of one mark, drawn by five launcher
         components with exactly one enabled — see `AppIconAliases`. The note is Android's
         own: this platform has no way to change an icon in place, and `settings-and-about`
         asks the reader to be told rather than left wondering. iOS confirms an icon change
         itself and says so in `appIcon.note`. Each platform states what its own system does,
         so the difference is deliberate, and `localization` / One state, one name calls a
         platform's own behaviour no divergence. -->
